<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kigeli IV Rwabugiri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1840–1895</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rwabugiri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kigeli IV Rwabugiri was mwami (king) of Rwanda in the second half of the 19th century and is regarded as its most powerful pre-colonial ruler. He centralised royal authority, weakened lineage chiefs, extended the system of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> clientage and led many military campaigns against neighbouring lands. He died in 1895, shortly before Rwanda came under German rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kigeli-iv-rwabugiri.jpg" alt="Kigeli IV Rwabugiri" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mwami_Kigeri_IV_Rwabugiri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
